Analysis by type of residence in Figure 13 demonstrates that urban and nomadic populations
have higher median ages at 17, while Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) have a lower median
age of 13. A possible explanation for this is that urban and nomadic populations tend to have
lower fertility rates, while IDP camps have a higher concentration of the younger and vulnerable
population, mainly young children compared to urban areas.
